<title>SOUTH AFRICA: WB Holdings yr share surges, div up.</title>
<headline>WB Holdings yr share surges, div up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     58     vs    23</p>
<p>    Div, total (cts)	18     vs     8</p>
<p>    Retained income	 18.85  vs    15.05</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   5.89   vs     2.11</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.40   vs     0.04 rebate</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.10   vs     0.01</p>
<p>    Gross revenue	  19.92   vs    14.09</p>
<p>Div payable: May 23</p>
<p>on register: April 18</p>
<p>Full name: WB Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The food group said fruit tonnage in 1997 would be lower than 1996 but it was anticipated that the weaker rand would compensate for some of the decline in tonnage.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
